        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hiwassee/Ocoee Scenic River State Park, Polk County, Tennessee, southern Appalachian Mountains, southeastern United States\n- Systems: Hiwassee River, Ocoee River, Toccoa River\n- Organizations: Tennessee state park\n\nFacts:\n- The Toccoa River and Ocoee River are two names for a single 93-mile river in the southeastern United States.\n- The Toccoa/Ocoee River flows northwestward through the southern Appalachian Mountains.\n- Hiwassee/Ocoee Scenic River State Park is a Tennessee state park in Polk County, Tennessee.\n- Hiwassee/Ocoee Scenic River State Park provides access to the Hiwassee River and the Ocoee River.",
